title: Genesis 11 – The Spirit of Babylon
description: A study from Genesis 11: Babel as the first one-world, works-based religion, spiritual whoredom against a jealous God, and the whore of Babylon in Revelation 17.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-11-spirit-of-babylon.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the separate Genesis 11 study of
# January 31, 2023 (posts 8240-8244), with the passages he gave from Exodus 34, Numbers 5, Deuteronomy 23, Matthew 19
# and Ezekiel 16.

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 11 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 11: The Spirit of Babylon
sub: A Jealous God • Spiritual Whoredom • The Whore of Babylon
refs: Genesis 11:4; Revelation 17:5
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The tower to Heaven
--- Let Us Build Us a Tower
kicker: vv. 1–4
sub: The First One-World Religion and Government
scripture: Genesis 11:1-4 | mark: let us build us a city and a tower, whose top may reach unto heaven; and let us make us a name
p: The original sin of the first one-world religion and government, just years after the flood, was to blaspheme God by building a tower to Heaven. Working their way to righteousness, that they may become as gods. [[lesson:genesis-11-tower-of-babel|The Tower of Babel]]

--- The Spirit of Babel
kicker: Genesis 11 • Revelation 17
sub: Adultery. Fornication. Whoredoms.
p: The study of Revelation 17 and the Whore of Babylon, and the fall of that wicked city, has a lot of context coming from scripture: concepts regarding the faithfulness of God, the betrothal to His people and the eventual marriage of the Lamb. There are many chapters and verses, but these should give you some ideas of this major theme throughout the Bible.
callout: The spirit of Babel, which is Babylon, and the empires and kingdoms that followed it, is one of adultery. Fornication. Whoredoms.

=== A jealous God
--- Whose Name Is Jealous
kicker: Cross references • Exodus 34
sub: Lest They Go a Whoring After Their Gods
scripture: Exodus 34:14-16 | mark: the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God; go a whoring after their gods
p: God has given us His law regarding marriage as a picture of His relationship with the saved. He is a jealous God. He speaks against idolatry and having other gods, the blasphemy of worshipping graven and molten images or other creatures in His stead, as fornication. Whoredoms. Harlotry. [[Exodus 34:6-7]]

--- The Spirit of Jealousy
kicker: Cross references • Exodus 34:14
fig: Numbers 5:30 | Numbers 5:30
fig: Deuteronomy 23:17 | Deuteronomy 23:17
callout: He draws parallel to actual whores: allowing the daughters of your land to commit fornication destroying a nation, with the destruction visited on those who forsake Him to chase after strange gods.

